───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
2. COMMERCIAL USE — PAID LICENSE REQUIRED
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

ANY business or commercial use — including use by for-profit organizations,
use in products or services offered to customers, internal commercial
tooling, and paid engagements — REQUIRES a commercial license from the
copyright holder. See COMMERCIAL-LICENSE.md for scope and contact.

There is no open-source grant for commercial use. Running Beagle at your
company without a commercial license is a license violation even if the use
is "internal only".

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
3. THE OPTIONAL beagle-orpheus WHEEL IS SEPARATELY LICENSED
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The `beagle-orpheus` wheel (native FlatBuffers-over-ring-buffer transport,
compiled C extension) is NOT covered by either license above. It is
proprietary software: free for evaluation and limited single-use trials,
and requires a paid license for any production or business deployment.
Downloading and installing it is an explicit, informed decision — beagle
ships and runs fully without it on the built-in HTTP transport.

See the beagle-orpheus distribution's own LICENSE for its terms.

